 Tell me pass or fail for each, and the exact text of any error.
+
+## T119. Connections screen and the Shopify form (0264)
+
+Setup: a register already connected to Shopify, with Zeller paired.
+
+1. More ▸ Settings ▸ **Connections**. Pass: every part of the till is listed, Shopify chosen for Catalogue, Stock, Discounts, Customers, Orders, Gift cards and Shared state (or iCloud if Cloud sync is on), Zeller for Connected terminal, and it says "Nothing saved: the till is using its current setup".
+2. Tap **Check connections**. Pass: "Every connection in use answered", or a plain line naming what is wrong.
+3. Go back without saving and make a test sale. Pass: nothing is different.
+4. Settings ▸ **Shopify** ▸ Save & test connection. Pass: "Connected to <shop name>. Scopes: ..." as before, and the location chips still appear.
+5. Switch Wi-Fi off and tap Save & test connection. Pass: it says "Could not connect: Could not reach Shopify. Check the internet connection and try again."
+6. Back in Connections tap **Off** under Stock, then **Save choice** and confirm. Pass: it says Saved, the Stock screens disappear or say stock is off, and sales still work. Tap **Go back to the current setup**. Pass: Stock returns.
+7. Try to switch Orders off. Pass: it is refused with a plain message.
+
+Tell me pass or fail for each, and the exact text of any error.
+
+## T120. Card reader through the Alloy (0265)
+
+Setup: a register with a Zeller reader paired, and practice mode available.
+
+1. Close and reopen the app. Make a card sale on the reader. Pass: it works exactly as before.
+2. Make a card refund on the reader. Pass: it works as before.
+3. More ▸ Support & diagnostics ▸ **Check reader**. Pass: "Reader ready" (or the usual reason when it is not).
+4. Diagnostics ▸ **Setup (pair terminal)**. Pass: "Paired" or the usual error text.
+5. Turn the reader off, then start a card sale. Pass: the usual "reader not ready" words, and the sale can still be paid by another way.
+6. In practice mode take a card payment and refund. Pass: the pretend reader answers and the real one is never touched.
+
+Tell me pass or fail for each, and the exact text of any error.
